WEBVTT

00:25.741 --> 00:30.078
FOOL NIGHT

01:49.574 --> 01:50.575
Die!

02:16.143 --> 02:17.769
<i>I have to go for his head.</i>

02:17.853 --> 02:19.771
<i>I don't care if we both get blown up.</i>

02:23.066 --> 02:24.442
Oh, wow.

02:24.526 --> 02:26.486
So you came here from Antarctica.

02:26.570 --> 02:28.196
That's so far away.

02:28.280 --> 02:30.365
And you call yourselves "Central"?

02:30.448 --> 02:32.367
It said that it's from Antarctica?

02:32.450 --> 02:35.537
That flower actually remembers
coming here from Antarctica?

02:36.413 --> 02:37.747
Uh, let me touch.

02:47.549 --> 02:50.051
You're doing a great job
out there, Mukuru.

02:50.135 --> 02:52.345
My life was extended once again.

03:34.888 --> 03:39.309
I guess Shiika is really gone
forever, isn't she?

03:39.851 --> 03:41.144
Yeah.

03:41.228 --> 03:44.689
All these flowers
are connected to people's lives.

03:44.773 --> 03:46.358
Everything that blooms here

03:46.441 --> 03:49.611
are only the memories and emotions
of those who are living.

03:49.694 --> 03:52.322
If Shiika had never been
turned into a desk,

03:52.405 --> 03:54.324
maybe I could've talked to her again.

03:56.952 --> 04:00.789
I finally found Shiika again,
but then I left her sitting in that alley.

04:00.872 --> 04:02.165
I need to go back now.

04:02.249 --> 04:04.251
I have to get her somewhere safe soon.

04:06.753 --> 04:08.421
It's time to say goodbye.

04:10.924 --> 04:13.718
Mister, do you think
that we can be friends?

04:17.514 --> 04:18.598
No, I don't.

04:19.808 --> 04:21.226
You can't forgive me?

04:22.227 --> 04:25.146
It just wouldn't be fair
to all of the people that you killed.

04:27.315 --> 04:30.110
You… need to be punished.

04:31.987 --> 04:35.198
Do you hate me…
for everything that I've done?

04:45.125 --> 04:47.377
Okay, I'm gonna go.

04:51.756 --> 04:55.802
Mister, the doctor and your girlfriend
are healing you right now.

04:55.885 --> 04:57.345
She's not my girlfriend.

04:57.429 --> 05:00.515
You'll probably wake up soon
and be able to return to your world.

05:05.770 --> 05:07.480
I hope that we can meet again.

05:22.037 --> 05:23.038
Mukuru!

05:31.171 --> 05:32.213
My name…

05:33.131 --> 05:34.674
My name is Toshiro Kamiya.

05:35.800 --> 05:38.845
It was just something
I wanted to tell you.

06:19.260 --> 06:20.178
You're awake!

06:21.429 --> 06:22.680
Oh!

06:22.764 --> 06:23.890
Thank goodness.

06:24.641 --> 06:25.975
I was so worried.

06:27.352 --> 06:28.895
Where's the doctor?

06:28.978 --> 06:32.232
Did the… Did the train stop?

06:33.525 --> 06:36.236
You just had a major surgery,
so don't push yourself.

06:37.654 --> 06:39.406
Okay, but what happened?

06:40.448 --> 06:41.825
Dr. Kudai escaped.

06:41.908 --> 06:42.992
Ivy did, too.

06:43.076 --> 06:46.162
He killed that guy in the snowsuit
who attacked us, then disappeared.

06:46.788 --> 06:49.874
But there's a ton of records
about Ivy's cultivation in this car.

06:49.958 --> 06:51.918
It's the proof we've been looking for.

06:52.001 --> 06:53.920
It shows that Dr. Kudai

06:54.003 --> 06:57.590
and the Anti-Transfloration Movement
created Ivy together.

06:57.674 --> 06:58.716
We got what we wanted.

06:58.800 --> 06:59.676
We really did it.

07:08.017 --> 07:10.645
Ugh, I'm seriously starving right now.

07:13.273 --> 07:14.482
<i>This just in.</i>

07:14.566 --> 07:17.360
<i>We received word that</i>
<i>Ken Hikasa of the Glory Days Party</i>

07:17.444 --> 07:20.363
<i>was involved in the research</i>
<i>for the killer Spiriflor.</i>

07:20.447 --> 07:22.782
<i>It was also confirmed</i>
<i>that Hikasa was found dead</i>

07:22.866 --> 07:24.659
<i>in an abandoned subway line.</i>

07:24.742 --> 07:26.161
<i>The documents seized by the police</i>

07:26.244 --> 07:29.747
<i>detail the Anti-Transfloration Movement's</i>
<i>financial support and communication</i>

07:29.831 --> 07:31.541
<i>- regarding research progress.</i>
- That can't be true!

07:31.624 --> 07:33.376
- Let's just get inside!
<i>- This suggests that there was</i>

07:33.460 --> 07:34.919
<i>a long-term plan in place.</i>

07:35.003 --> 07:36.671
- Don't listen to this!
<i>- The Glory Days Party issued</i>

07:36.754 --> 07:40.300
<i>a statement saying, "This was an act</i>
<i>conducted by Hikasa alone.</i>

07:40.383 --> 07:41.718
<i>The party had no involvement."</i>

07:41.801 --> 07:44.262
<i>But it has sent shockwaves</i>
<i>throughout the political world.</i>

08:22.592 --> 08:24.761
ABOLISH TRANSFLORATION!

08:29.224 --> 08:32.018
<i>The frequent protests</i>
<i>by the Anti-Transfloration Movement</i>

08:32.101 --> 08:34.354
<i>are gradually dying down.</i>

08:34.437 --> 08:36.981
<i>The Movement's political party,</i>
<i>the Glory Days Party,</i>

08:37.065 --> 08:38.608
<i>has just announced its dissolution--</i>

08:55.250 --> 08:58.336
Dr. Kudai, why did you create Ivy?

08:58.419 --> 09:01.089
Who was that armed guy in the snow suit
that attacked us?

09:01.172 --> 09:02.966
Why did you erase your name?

09:03.049 --> 09:05.260
You took it off of
every document out there.

09:05.343 --> 09:07.262
What exactly are you fighting against?

09:07.345 --> 09:09.681
Why on earth would I give
those answers to you,

09:09.764 --> 09:12.517
someone who's a member
of an enemy organization?

09:13.768 --> 09:17.272
If we knew the truth about everything,
maybe we could finally stop being enemies.

09:17.355 --> 09:20.275
First and foremost,
I've been in hiding this entire time

09:20.358 --> 09:22.902
because I don't want the world
to know that I'm still alive.

09:23.570 --> 09:27.031
Whether I decide to have you killed or not
doesn't really matter now.

09:27.115 --> 09:29.158
My research is scattered
all over the tracks,

09:29.242 --> 09:31.411
so it's only a matter of time
before it's exposed.

09:33.246 --> 09:34.289
I just had a great idea!

09:35.248 --> 09:38.042
I want you to become my own personal spy.

09:38.751 --> 09:40.003
In fact, that's my condition

09:40.086 --> 09:43.298
if you want me to answer
any of the questions you have.

09:43.381 --> 09:47.051
Your first mission for me is to find out
who created your friend here.

09:49.596 --> 09:51.472
<i>Toshiro was created?</i>

09:51.556 --> 09:54.434
<i>His powers aren't random,</i>
<i>someone made him that way?</i>

09:54.517 --> 09:55.643
<i>Why?</i>

09:55.727 --> 09:58.104
<i>And I would have to be Dr. Kudai's spy?</i>

09:59.230 --> 10:00.481
<i>I could never.</i>

10:01.399 --> 10:02.692
<i>But if I refuse,</i>

10:03.693 --> 10:07.363
<i>Ivy will come back and Toshiro and I will…</i>

10:07.989 --> 10:12.869
By the way, I should clarify that I don't
want to do anything to Transflora Medical.

10:12.952 --> 10:15.830
However, if they were
to destroy themselves on their own,

10:15.913 --> 10:19.208
I'd be very, very much in favor of that!

10:21.419 --> 10:24.797
All I want now is to give the future
of humanity one more option.

10:24.881 --> 10:26.215
I think we owe it to them.

10:28.426 --> 10:30.178
So now you have to make a decision.

10:30.261 --> 10:32.096
Will you be my spy or not?

10:34.098 --> 10:35.850
It'll determine whether you live or die.

10:47.070 --> 10:49.238
Okay. Well then, ask me anything you want.

10:49.322 --> 10:51.449
Why do you even want me to be your spy?

10:51.532 --> 10:54.744
Because I would like to be able
to speak to and work

10:54.827 --> 10:56.829
with the brilliant researcher
who created Toshiro.

10:56.913 --> 11:00.166
You just said that Transflora Medical
is your enemy.

11:00.249 --> 11:02.251
Toshiro underwent Transfloration there,

11:02.335 --> 11:04.879
so doesn't that make
that researcher your enemy?

11:05.546 --> 11:07.382
You're quite the clever one, aren't you?

11:07.465 --> 11:10.301
Well, I can't afford to worry
about things like that anymore.

11:12.303 --> 11:14.055
As you can see, my time's limited,

11:14.138 --> 11:16.307
so I intend to make
the most of what's left.

11:23.940 --> 11:28.945
You… underwent Transfloration?

11:29.779 --> 11:32.699
- But what are you doing?
- By clipping away the parts of organs

11:32.782 --> 11:36.160
that have been encroached upon,
I'm delaying the Transfloration.

11:36.244 --> 11:37.286
I can't cut the trunk,

11:37.370 --> 11:40.206
but cutting the branches and leaves
isn't a problem.

11:41.249 --> 11:45.002
I've been living like this for three years
since I underwent the procedure.

11:45.086 --> 11:47.588
Unfortunately, I've just about
reached my limit.

11:48.673 --> 11:52.677
Also, the researcher who created Toshiro
most likely isn't my enemy.

11:52.760 --> 11:54.637
I think we may have the same goal.

11:54.721 --> 11:55.680
Huh?

11:55.763 --> 11:59.308
His research goes against
the principles of Transflora Medical.

11:59.392 --> 12:01.394
Either he conducts his research in secret,

12:01.477 --> 12:03.896
hiding it from them,
or he works independently.

12:03.980 --> 12:06.649
What do you mean by their "principles?"

12:06.733 --> 12:08.234
Producing oxygen?

12:08.317 --> 12:09.444
Yes, of course.

12:09.527 --> 12:12.071
That is one of their
major goals, isn't it?

12:12.864 --> 12:16.826
First, let me briefly explain to you
how Transflora Medical came to be.

12:18.327 --> 12:20.621
Around the year 2200,

12:20.705 --> 12:22.957
the world became covered in thick clouds,

12:23.040 --> 12:25.543
blocking out the sunlight
that was essential to life.

12:25.626 --> 12:27.044
Plants and trees withered,

12:27.128 --> 12:31.090
and we were no longer able to get
accurate information from our satellites.

12:31.174 --> 12:33.634
That's when the endless night
and winter began.

12:34.927 --> 12:37.388
<i>Earth was in danger</i>
<i>of running out of oxygen.</i>

12:37.472 --> 12:40.516
<i>In response,</i>
<i>the world's top bio-researchers</i>

12:40.600 --> 12:42.643
<i>were brought together to find a solution.</i>

12:42.727 --> 12:45.897
<i>A research institute was</i>
<i>created for them called Central.</i>

12:46.773 --> 12:48.149
<i>Their research produced results</i>

12:48.232 --> 12:51.235
<i>and they succeeded in developing</i>
<i>Transfloration technology.</i>

12:51.319 --> 12:55.531
<i>As you know, it repurposes the human body</i>
<i>for environmental conservation.</i>

12:56.199 --> 12:58.159
However, the researchers at Central

12:58.242 --> 13:00.995
refused to undergo
Transfloration themselves.

13:01.078 --> 13:02.705
They said someone else could do it

13:02.789 --> 13:06.626
and they shut themselves away
from the rest of society in Antarctica.

13:06.709 --> 13:07.877
Cowardly, right?

13:07.960 --> 13:11.506
They're a bunch of narrow-minded idiots,
clinging to their human forms.

13:12.131 --> 13:14.091
<i>Central is eagerly awaiting the day</i>

13:14.175 --> 13:17.929
<i>when everyone across the continents</i>
<i>has undergone Transfloration,</i>

13:18.012 --> 13:20.306
<i>so that hundreds of years from now,</i>

13:20.389 --> 13:24.268
<i>they can once again set foot</i>
<i>on lush, green land as humans.</i>

13:25.394 --> 13:27.230
The truth is that Transflora Medical,

13:27.313 --> 13:29.023
along with the Transfloration Board,

13:29.106 --> 13:31.859
are nothing more than
plant production factories,

13:31.943 --> 13:34.737
built to realize
Central's ultimate vision.

13:36.405 --> 13:38.741
But, I will say, if it weren't for them,

13:38.825 --> 13:41.244
we would have died
from oxygen deprivation.

13:41.327 --> 13:43.955
So, I suppose we can't
hate them too much, right?

13:44.664 --> 13:45.665
But that's…

13:46.582 --> 13:49.126
For the sake of that vision,
they're now trying to stop

13:49.210 --> 13:51.754
the further development
of Transfloration technology.

13:52.380 --> 13:56.592
They're forcing us to accept this fate
and obediently turn into plants.

13:56.676 --> 13:59.262
I won't sit idly by
and allow them to do that.

14:01.806 --> 14:04.392
The evolution of humanity
is just around the corner,

14:04.475 --> 14:07.144
it's no longer some distant possibility.

14:08.312 --> 14:10.439
We are about to enter into a new age

14:10.523 --> 14:13.067
where more people like
Toshiro and Mukuru exist.

14:13.150 --> 14:16.445
Finding the person who performed
Transfloration on Toshiro

14:16.529 --> 14:18.364
will help bring about that new era.

14:18.447 --> 14:20.241
Isn't that magnificent?

14:20.324 --> 14:24.537
So does that mean that guy in the snowsuit
was sent here by Central to attack you?

14:24.620 --> 14:25.997
Indeed.

14:26.080 --> 14:27.748
They sent him all the way here

14:27.832 --> 14:30.251
and he couldn't even manage
to kill one old man.

14:30.334 --> 14:32.503
- Doctor!
- Sorry, time's up.

14:33.212 --> 14:36.340
I'll be sending someone
over to you eventually

14:36.424 --> 14:39.802
to collect whatever information
you gain from spying.

14:42.889 --> 14:46.058
Oh, by the way, you never did
tell me your name, my dear.

14:47.268 --> 14:48.644
It's Yomiko Horai.

14:49.145 --> 14:50.771
Yomiko.

14:50.855 --> 14:52.523
Child of the ferryman to Hell.

14:52.607 --> 14:55.318
A name fit for
a Transflora Medical employee.

14:55.401 --> 14:56.527
Here's a souvenir.

15:01.866 --> 15:03.242
I have no use for it.

15:30.478 --> 15:31.312
TRANSFLORA MEDICAL

15:31.395 --> 15:35.149
So, you're the ones at the center of it,
all of this commotion.

15:36.734 --> 15:39.862
You did well to stop
the Anti-Transfloration Movement

15:39.946 --> 15:41.530
and clear us of suspicion.

15:41.614 --> 15:42.698
Thank you.

15:42.782 --> 15:44.116
Of course, sir.

15:44.200 --> 15:45.701
Director Kikuoka.

15:45.785 --> 15:49.372
About the fight earlier, will there be
a trial or compensatory damages?

15:49.455 --> 15:51.707
You don't need to worry about that.

15:51.791 --> 15:53.125
We'll deal with it all.

15:53.793 --> 15:56.337
No individual will be held responsible.

15:57.755 --> 16:00.174
However, I would like
to reward each of you

16:00.257 --> 16:01.384
for everything you've done.

16:01.467 --> 16:05.137
If there's anything I can do for you,
please just say the word.

16:08.724 --> 16:09.684
Toshiro Kamiya!

16:09.767 --> 16:11.018
Saeko Kanaeno.

16:11.102 --> 16:14.355
- Make her a Transflora Medical employee!
- Make him a Transflora Medical employee!

16:15.189 --> 16:16.065
Hmm?

16:18.526 --> 16:19.944
And you, Hiragishi?

16:26.283 --> 16:27.910
I appreciate the offer,

16:27.994 --> 16:31.622
but would it be possible for me
to put that on hold for the time being?

16:32.331 --> 16:34.917
You're saying you want me
to owe you a favor?

16:35.835 --> 16:37.336
Will that be an issue?

16:40.089 --> 16:41.590
Very well, then.

16:42.466 --> 16:44.260
JOB OFFER LETTER

16:53.769 --> 16:56.480
Takami, Asada, Yorutake.

16:56.564 --> 16:57.732
Thank you.

16:58.691 --> 17:00.776
We'll enjoy this for all of you, too.

17:03.654 --> 17:05.614
You guys did a great job.

17:05.698 --> 17:07.908
Though, it was pretty dumb
for the white-haired kid

17:07.992 --> 17:10.202
to charge into the subway unarmed.

17:10.286 --> 17:12.705
I think that everyone did great.

17:12.788 --> 17:15.416
Thank you for protecting
Transflora Medical Number 4.

17:15.499 --> 17:17.376
Yomiko and Toshiro.

17:18.335 --> 17:20.504
You fought for all of us. Thank you.

17:20.588 --> 17:22.798
I can't believe you actually did it.

17:23.382 --> 17:25.551
All right, you guys.

17:28.012 --> 17:29.055
Let's drink!

17:50.284 --> 17:51.202
<i>This is fun.</i>

17:52.953 --> 17:54.538
<i>I'm so happy.</i>

17:55.372 --> 17:57.124
<i>I hope this party never ends.</i>

17:58.125 --> 18:00.002
<i>I wish time could just stop.</i>

18:02.046 --> 18:03.923
<i>I don't want to become a Spiriflor.</i>

18:05.257 --> 18:06.926
<i>I want to be like this.</i>

18:08.594 --> 18:11.347
<i>With everyone, forever.</i>

18:17.812 --> 18:18.938
I'm home.

18:58.394 --> 19:00.396
I think I might be losing my mind.

19:26.922 --> 19:31.927
TRANSFLORA MEDICAL

19:46.066 --> 19:47.318
Ms. Horai.

19:47.401 --> 19:50.321
There's someone in room six
applying for Transfloration.

19:51.030 --> 19:52.114
Okay.

20:08.964 --> 20:10.841
TRANSFLORATION REPORT
MEG OKUMURA

20:11.550 --> 20:14.887
She's from Paupertown. From the Parade.

20:14.970 --> 20:16.096
It's coming.

20:18.015 --> 20:19.099
The morning is.

20:22.186 --> 20:23.520
Morning is coming.

20:27.191 --> 20:28.234
Morning is…

20:41.163 --> 20:44.708
Please, shine on everyone

20:45.459 --> 20:48.337
with love and with light.

20:52.591 --> 20:53.676
This girl.

20:54.426 --> 20:55.594
Not this girl.

20:57.763 --> 20:58.847
You're okay.

21:08.732 --> 21:14.613
PATIENT: KAORI KAMIYA
VISITOR: TOSHIRO KAMIYA

21:20.202 --> 21:23.539
Your mother is resting
in the high-intensity light room.

21:24.832 --> 21:26.959
She seems to feel restless in the dark.

21:28.294 --> 21:29.545
I understand.

21:56.697 --> 21:57.948
Hello, Mother.

21:59.491 --> 22:00.826
It's been a while.

22:11.795 --> 22:15.591
I'm not… I'm not the one you should blame.

22:16.800 --> 22:18.635
I was being deceived.

22:18.719 --> 22:20.679
I couldn't help losing my temper.

22:22.348 --> 22:25.768
Someone has been hiding
the sunlight from us all.

22:25.851 --> 22:28.354
I won't be deceived any longer.

22:35.986 --> 22:36.945
You know…

22:38.739 --> 22:39.948
I have…

22:40.032 --> 22:43.577
I have this feeling that
I know what I should do now.

22:46.121 --> 22:47.915
I'm going to help other people.

22:52.586 --> 22:53.587
Yeah.

22:54.213 --> 22:55.756
Mm. Mm.

22:56.173 --> 22:57.716
Mm-hmm.

23:01.929 --> 23:03.097
Okay, got it.

23:03.180 --> 23:04.598
I'm on my way.
